    "created_at": "2023-07-04T07:22:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-07-04T07:22:20Z",
    "body": "For Blink, the limit does not apply to JavaScript code, i.e. `/(\\d+)*$/.exec(\"0000011111111111111000z\")`. It does though apply in WebKit.\r\n\r\nOnly Blinks `ScriptRegexp` [constructor](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/script_regexp.cc;l=43;bpv=1;bpt=1?q=ScriptRegexp&ss=chromium) applies the backtracking limit and seems to be used only for C++-side regexes.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
